Ported from ../outln/__tests__/cases/typescript/008-glob-view-multiple-globs.case.yaml; expected output is the TypeScript build's.
Its source-code inputs were rewritten as Markdown files.
Except: the glob view says "a header or summary" instead of "header comments" (docs/changelog.md).
== args
input/a/**/*
input/**/*
== file input/a/one.md
---
description: One summary.
---
# one
== file input/a/two.md
---
title: Some title
summary: Two summary.
---
== file input/z/three.md
---
description: Three summary.
---
# three
== stdout
glob view: input/a/**/* input/**/*
Includes only a header or summary per file.
For file-level outlines, use `outln [FILE]...`.
input/a/one.md: description: "One summary."
input/a/two.md: title: "Some title", summary: "Two summary."
input/z/three.md: description: "Three summary."
